  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 5, ‘Share of countries by the number of occupations for which stock data is available on the NHWA data platform’ (Source: WHO National Health Workforce Accounts, 2025). A 100% stacked horizontal bar chart across five categories (5 or less occupations, 6 to 10, 11 to 20, 21 to 30, and 31 or more occupations) for Global, the six WHO regions (AFR, AMR, SEAR, EUR, EMR, WPR), and the four World Bank income groups (HIC, UMIC, LMIC, LIC). Globally, 1% of countries have stock data for 5 or fewer occupations, 21% for 6 to 10, 29% for 11 to 20, 29% for 21 to 30, and 21% for 31 or more occupations.",
